.TH DATE 1 "2026-11-17" "nova-cli 0.20.0" "NovaOS"
.SH NAME
date \- Display or set civil time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B date
[OPTION]... [+FORMAT]
.br
.B date
MMDDhhmm[[CC]YY][.ss]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the current clock, parse an input date, or format the
modification time of a selected file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-d STRING, \-\-date=STRING"
Read STRING. An argument starting with @ denotes seconds since
the Unix epoch. Negative and fractional values are accepted.
.TP
.B "\-f FILE, \-\-file=FILE"
Read one input date per line. A single dash selects standard
input. Invalid lines are diagnosed while processing continues.
.TP
.B "\-r FILE, \-\-reference=FILE"
Use the modification time of FILE.
.TP
.B "\-s STRING, \-\-set=STRING"
Request a clock change. The native ABI v1 rejects this
request.
.TP
.B "\-u, \-\-uct, \-\-utc, \-\-universal"
Use UTC for input and output.
.TP
.B "\-I[PREC], \-\-iso\-8601[=PREC]"
Print an ISO date. With an attached precision, print date,
hours, minutes, seconds or ns.
.TP
.B "\-R, \-\-rfc\-email, \-\-rfc\-822, \-\-rfc\-2822"
Format an RFC email date.
.TP
.B "\-\-rfc\-3339=PREC"
Select date, seconds or ns precision.
.TP
.B "\-\-resolution"
Print the clock resolution.
.TP
.B "\-\-debug"
Describe parsing on standard error.
.TP
.B "\-\-help, \-\-version"
Display help or the version and exit.
.SH "Access and exit status"
Documentation uses no file or clock grant. A selected file
requires a read grant. NovaOS v1 provides a UTC clock in whole
seconds. Success returns 0. Operational and usage errors
return 1.
.SH Examples
.nf
date \-u \-d @0 '+%F %T %Z'
date \-Ins \-d 2024\-02\-29
date \-f \- '+%s.%N'
.fi
